# Owner review is required on the AI configuration itself. If you fork or
# generate a new repo from this template, replace @alfredobs97 below with
# your own GitHub username or team.
#
# `AGENTS.md` is hand-written, not generated — it is the project's
# conventions guide for humans and agents alike. `ai/agents/*.yaml`,
# `ai/workflows/*.md`, `ai/mcp.yaml` and `.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md` are the
# other hand-written sources; `tool/sync_ai_config.dart` renders everything
# else under `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.opencode/`, `opencode.jsonc`, and
# `.agents/agents|workflows|rules|mcp_config.json` from them — see
# ai/README.md. An unreviewed edit to any of these hand-written sources can
# silently change how every subagent, MCP server and workflow behaves, so
# it is worth requiring an explicit reviewer rather than letting it merge
# like ordinary code. Uncomment and fill in the lines below to enable this
# protection.
#
# `tool/hooks/format_changed.dart` and `.pi/extensions/` are a different,
# higher-stakes category: they are executable code that a harness runs
# automatically (a Claude Code PostToolUse hook, a Pi extension) on every
# contributor's machine once trusted — not just config a harness reads.
# Covering them here means executable harness code can't merge without an
# explicit reviewer, the same reasoning as reviewing a CI workflow change.

/ai/ @alfredobs97
/.agents/skills/ @alfredobs97
/AGENTS.md @alfredobs97
/packages/*/AGENTS.md @alfredobs97
/tool/hooks/ @alfredobs97
/.pi/extensions/ @alfredobs97
